{
  "slug": "claude-todo-mirror",
  "name": "Claude Todo Mirror",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Mirrors Claude Code's TodoWrite state to per-session Markdown files with hierarchical checkboxes ([x] / [▶] / [ ]). Pin the file in VS Code, Obsidian, or any Markdown viewer for an always-visible task view — no more scrolling back through chat to see what's left. Includes per-session isolation, a multi-session index, and slash commands (/todos-watch, /todos-pause, /todos-resume) for managing the mirror.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Commands** (3): `todos-pause` (Pause TodoWrite markdown mirroring for this project (creates .paused flag)), `todos-resume` (Resume TodoWrite markdown mirroring for this project (removes .paused flag)), `todos-watch` (Open a new Terminal window that live-watches this project's TodoWrite mirror files (macOS only))\n- **Hooks** (1): `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-todo-mirror@claude-community` from `bighaeil/claude-todo-mirror`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 1,
    "command": 3
  },
